WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.230
I asked my helper to book a

2
00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:04.470
bus ticket to the city.

3
00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:07.860
It said: sorry, I can’t do that!

4
00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:09.350
Was it being lazy?

5
00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:12.370
No: it just didn’t have that tool.

6
00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:16.070
Today: a helper and its toolbox.

7
00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.120
A helper has a toolbox.

8
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:22.940
Darsi Tiny has ten tools: the weather,

9
00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:25.280
a calculator, the timetable,

10
00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:28.680
reminders, a route finder, and more.

11
00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.840
It can only do the jobs its tools can do.

12
00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:34.570
For each question, it picks

13
00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:35.550
the tool that fits.

14
00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:37.620
How far is it to Dala?

15
00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:38.890
The route tool.

16
00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:42.020
What is seventeen times twenty-three?

17
00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:43.280
The calculator.

18
00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:47.130
When no tool fits the job, a

19
00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:48.210
good helper says so.

20
00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:49.450
Book a ticket?

21
00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:52.680
I can’t: none of my tools can do that.

22
00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:54.990
That’s honest, and that’s good!

23
00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:57.760
And when something is

24
00:00:57.760 --> 00:00:59.160
missing, it asks you.

25
00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:00.930
What’s the weather tomorrow?

26
00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:02.140
Which village?

27
00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:05.460
Once you say Dala, it uses

28
00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:06.240
the weather tool.

29
00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:07.970
Quick check!

30
00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:12.520
You ask: will it rain in Sabo tomorrow?

31
00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:15.620
Which tool should the helper pick?

32
00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:18.800
The weather tool, with the place,

33
00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:21.640
Sabo, and the day, tomorrow.

34
00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:24.340
A tool needs the right details,

35
00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:26.000
like a form you fill in.

36
00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:28.770
Helpers can still guess wrong.

37
00:01:29.470 --> 00:01:31.870
I asked about class 9Z,

38
00:01:32.230 --> 00:01:33.470
which doesn’t exist.

39
00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:37.600
Darsi Tiny wrote 9C, a different class!

40
00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:39.710
So check what it filled in.

41
00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:43.360
In the app, you can switch tools off.

42
00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:46.410
Ask for the weather, then switch the

43
00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:48.290
weather tool off and ask again.

44
00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:50.540
What does the helper say now?

45
00:01:51.790 --> 00:01:52.550
Your turn.

46
00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:55.470
You ask the helper to buy you new

47
00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:58.230
shoes, but it has no shopping tool.

48
00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:00.430
What should a good helper say?

49
00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:04.320
Sorry, I can’t: that’s the honest answer.

50
00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:07.130
Remember: a helper picks

51
00:02:07.130 --> 00:02:08.330
the tool that fits.

52
00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:11.590
With no tool, it says I can’t.

53
00:02:12.130 --> 00:02:14.410
And when something is missing, it asks.

54
00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:17.780
Try it yourself: make a toolbox

55
00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:18.940
of cards with a friend.

56
00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:21.740
Write one tool on each card:

57
00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:24.900
weather, calculator, timetable.

58
00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:28.120
Your friend asks things, and you pick a

59
00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:31.940
card, ask what’s missing, or say I can’t!
